# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production build configuration.
#
# Vite reads this automatically for `npm run build` (mode=production) and
# IGNORES it during `npm run dev`, so local development is unaffected — there
# the API is reached through the dev proxy in vite.config.js instead.
#
# NOTHING SECRET BELONGS HERE. Every VITE_ variable is inlined into the
# JavaScript served to every visitor. This file is tracked in git precisely
# because it is public: it pins the API address the production bundle compiles
# against, so any machine that builds produces the same bundle.
#
# THESE ARE BUILD-TIME VALUES. Changing one requires a rebuild and re-upload;
# editing it on the server does nothing, because the value is already baked
# into the JavaScript.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# THE "/api/v1" SUFFIX IS PART OF THE ADDRESS — do not drop it.
#
# The API mounts every route under API_PREFIX, which defaults to /api/v1. Built
# against the bare origin, the app asks for /auth/login instead of
# /api/v1/auth/login and EVERY request returns 404: login, register, categories,
# products, promotions, settings. The site loads perfectly and nothing works,
# which reads as a broken backend rather than a missing path segment.
#
# If the API_PREFIX on the server is ever changed, change it here too — these
# two values are one setting written in two places.
VITE_API_URL=https://featherbonepk-production.up.railway.app/api/v1

VITE_APP_NAME=Feather & Bone
VITE_CURRENCY=PKR
